{"concept":"courage","groups":[{"id":"dispositions","name":{"ru":"Печаль, досада, смирение и гордость","en":"Melancholy, discontent, humility and pride"},"count":25},{"id":"courage","name":{"ru":"Мужество и храбрость","en":"Courage and bravery"},"count":33},{"id":"neighbour-words","name":{"ru":"Догадка, неожиданность и грация","en":"Conjecture, surprise and grace"},"count":6},{"id":"exuberance","name":{"ru":"Избыток и озорство","en":"Excess and exuberance"},"count":19}],"occurrences":[{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-a590b524693bb058d30f6d26cdc7270f","tos.text-unit.sid-a590b524693bb058d30f6d26cdc7270f"]},"form":"Hochmuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["agency","zarathustra","camel"],"line":{"ru":"Тяжесть духа — унизиться, чтобы заставить страдать своё высокомерие.","en":"The spirit’s burden is to humble oneself in order to make one’s pride suffer."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6ff057cbfa5323c0c554f447ed37cf36","tos.text-unit.sid-6ff057cbfa5323c0c554f447ed37cf36"]},"form":"muthig","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["will","identity","creation","laughter","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество хочет смеяться и создаёт себе горных духов.","en":"Courage wants to laugh and creates goblins for itself."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1bb9a00dacec240301d68cb560ebf58b","tos.text-unit.sid-1bb9a00dacec240301d68cb560ebf58b"]},"form":"Muthig","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мудрость любит воина и хочет видеть нас беззаботными, насмешливыми и сильными.","en":"Wisdom loves the warrior and wants us carefree, mocking and strong."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.10","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-94b1fe7ed5c9fd941d159b5c42aa564e","tos.text-unit.sid-94b1fe7ed5c9fd941d159b5c42aa564e"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["bite","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Смертная усталость ждёт случайного конца со стиснутыми зубами.","en":"Deathly weariness waits with clenched teeth for a chance ending."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6ae75f66e2fa5944e659f4f1dcaa4d90","tos.text-unit.sid-6ae75f66e2fa5944e659f4f1dcaa4d90"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["agency","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Война и мужество совершили великие дела, а храбрость спасала несчастных.","en":"War and courage accomplished great deeds, and bravery saved the unfortunate."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1a580258fcbabd5f64363b7242f4afd4","tos.text-unit.sid-1a580258fcbabd5f64363b7242f4afd4"]},"form":"Tapfer","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra","little-girls"],"line":{"ru":"Воинам сказано: хорошо быть храбрым.","en":"Warriors are offered the good of bravery."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-758d2ab29c2890daa190ba4f136aa23f","tos.text-unit.sid-758d2ab29c2890daa190ba4f136aa23f"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Единичный человек пока хранит мужество и надежды среди многих.","en":"The individual still keeps courage and hopes among the many."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-569f2bbd7c7f34d53bc310b5d8f4fdc5","tos.text-unit.sid-569f2bbd7c7f34d53bc310b5d8f4fdc5"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["becoming","circle","loneliness","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Одиночество способно утомить гордость и мужество.","en":"Solitude can weary pride and courage."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.19","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-cf11680770dae35b86100e999fc7332b","tos.text-unit.sid-cf11680770dae35b86100e999fc7332b"]},"form":"Tapferkeit","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"old-woman","mode":"quoted","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Любовь призвана храбро идти навстречу страшному.","en":"Love is called to advance bravely toward what frightens it."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-f13f09e8ff15893d7695a59b6bb6d752","tos.text-unit.sid-f13f09e8ff15893d7695a59b6bb6d752"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра связывает раннюю тоску по смерти с печалью Иисуса.","en":"Zarathustra joins early longing for death to Jesus’ sadness."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"I.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-d011a82fc32d99a3cdc7ef437c7cb537","tos.text-unit.sid-d011a82fc32d99a3cdc7ef437c7cb537"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["child","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Зрелый мужчина сохраняет больше детства и меньше печали.","en":"The mature man retains more childhood and less sadness."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-2a9d12552e21d7aa8cbb46bf849cf165","tos.text-unit.sid-2a9d12552e21d7aa8cbb46bf849cf165"]},"form":"Muthmaassung","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["will","creation","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра хочет, чтобы предположение не простиралось дальше созидающей воли слушателя.","en":"The teacher bounds conjecture by the listener’s creative will."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1658712a9a10763f50395724d416ae08","tos.text-unit.sid-1658712a9a10763f50395724d416ae08"]},"form":"Muthmaassung","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра хочет, чтобы предположение о Боге было ограничено мыслимостью.","en":"Conjecture is bounded by thinkability."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-981af960d1bdf16da0e3eb48454a1005","tos.text-unit.sid-981af960d1bdf16da0e3eb48454a1005"]},"form":"Muthmaassung","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["creation","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра спрашивает, кто выдержит муку предположения о Боге и не умрёт.","en":"Zarathustra asks who could endure the anguish of the supposition of God and not die."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-f8faeb4f7654219625525b903620ce97","tos.text-unit.sid-f8faeb4f7654219625525b903620ce97"]},"form":"muthmaassen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Отрицание преходящего переживается телом как головокружение.","en":"Denying transience is experienced bodily as vertigo."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6518d675717bd45c650266cb62f66d66","tos.text-unit.sid-6518d675717bd45c650266cb62f66d66"]},"form":"Demuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Смирение жрецов названо мстительным.","en":"The priests’ humility is called revengeful."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-c6e5d7fe4eb63451f8c04ca42d9fcb86","tos.text-unit.sid-c6e5d7fe4eb63451f8c04ca42d9fcb86"]},"form":"unmuthig","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Отвращение к прошлому и настоящему переживается через запах.","en":"Disgust at past and present is experienced through smell."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-10d6cba4bce5fa00e9d65dbf56b3af07","tos.text-unit.sid-10d6cba4bce5fa00e9d65dbf56b3af07"]},"form":"Übermuthe","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Могущественный господин допускает рабское своеволие.","en":"The powerful master permits the slave’s exuberance."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.13","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5189a087d94914fd8bbe02818277bd72","tos.text-unit.sid-5189a087d94914fd8bbe02818277bd72"]},"form":"Anmuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["attention","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Красота входит в великодушие возвышенно настроенных.","en":"Beauty enters into the generosity of the sublimely minded."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-eacfb2c146f965b9faf6bd963d67805e","tos.text-unit.sid-eacfb2c146f965b9faf6bd963d67805e"]},"form":"Unmuthe","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"dispositions"},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.20","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1857c18c3f1848a0473d8e41f2ae1356","tos.text-unit.sid-1857c18c3f1848a0473d8e41f2ae1356"]},"form":"Unmuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["identity","revenge","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Воля мстит тому, кто не разделяет её гнева и досады.","en":"The will takes revenge on those who do not share its anger and vexation."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.21","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-fc1772d347206aeec5e62aea8ed0f048","tos.text-unit.sid-fc1772d347206aeec5e62aea8ed0f048"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Театральность тщеславных лечит учительскую печаль.","en":"The vain people’s theatricality heals the teacher’s melancholy."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.21","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-2290a81470148fb166fab9e44bae2808","tos.text-unit.sid-2290a81470148fb166fab9e44bae2808"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Тщеславные удерживают учителя возле человеческого зрелища.","en":"The vain keep the teacher near the human spectacle."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-604b842c7cf2378104f0f2bb0f47cfc1","tos.text-unit.sid-604b842c7cf2378104f0f2bb0f47cfc1"]},"form":"Demuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"dream","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra","quietest-hour"],"line":{"ru":"Тишайший час говорит учителю, что он ещё недостаточно кроток.","en":"The stillest hour demands a deeper humility."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"II.22","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-7c2ee6a58e968b3d3e1987ed4e4e882e","tos.text-unit.sid-7c2ee6a58e968b3d3e1987ed4e4e882e"]},"form":"Demuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"disciples","mode":"dream","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель отвечает знанием собственных долин.","en":"The teacher answers with knowledge of his own valleys."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.01","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-01f6a3ba6565c1fb8483cd4e0fa16cd3","tos.text-unit.sid-01f6a3ba6565c1fb8483cd4e0fa16cd3"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Высшее мужество принимает путь без дороги назад.","en":"The highest courage accepts a path with no way back."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.01","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5dbcb9a058383b8f84f979f7dbfef21c","tos.text-unit.sid-5dbcb9a058383b8f84f979f7dbfef21c"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["will","identity","laughter"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель смеётся над собственным утешением моря.","en":"The teacher laughs at his own consoling of the sea."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-7bb0c3706146f1049d8b36a8192e9967","tos.text-unit.sid-7bb0c3706146f1049d8b36a8192e9967"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество убивает уныние и заставляет Заратустру бросить вызов карлику.","en":"Courage kills despondency and makes Zarathustra challenge the dwarf."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-02327647178ad8d7fe89b718b92e7c64","tos.text-unit.sid-02327647178ad8d7fe89b718b92e7c64"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["innocence-play","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Нападающее мужество названо лучшим смертоносным оружием; в каждом нападении звучит победная музыка.","en":"Attacking courage is called the best slayer; in every attack there is triumphant music."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9bbeafa4156f9fa420ff9272484687b6","tos.text-unit.sid-9bbeafa4156f9fa420ff9272484687b6"]},"form":"muthigste","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["innocence-play","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество человека победило животных, а победная музыка преодолела всякое страдание.","en":"Human courage conquered the animals, and triumphant music overcame every suffering."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5580aa08306224ddbe2b2e3cc9fc1938","tos.text-unit.sid-5580aa08306224ddbe2b2e3cc9fc1938"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["identity","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество побеждает головокружение на краю пропасти; заглянуть в себя — значит заглянуть в пропасть.","en":"Courage overcomes dizziness at the abyss; looking into oneself is looking into an abyss."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-8ae25a5f2dc31de3ca142de8f588edc2","tos.text-unit.sid-8ae25a5f2dc31de3ca142de8f588edc2"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество убивает жалость; заглядывая в жизнь, человек заглядывает и в страдание.","en":"Courage kills pity; looking into life, one also looks into suffering."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.02","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-54f0be3cffb65e366d441fbeab603bb5","tos.text-unit.sid-54f0be3cffb65e366d441fbeab603bb5"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"sailors","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество убивает смерть словами: «Так это была жизнь? Ну, что ж! Ещё раз!»","en":"Courage overcomes death by calling for life once more."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.03","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-458147866d49668a411c35a98782cc56","tos.text-unit.sid-458147866d49668a411c35a98782cc56"]},"form":"Übermuthe","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","lion","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Призыв тяжёлой мысли требует львиного избытка силы.","en":"Summoning the heavy thought requires a lion’s excess of strength."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-f5bfc91bb67aca2f0758c4e4166ac242","tos.text-unit.sid-f5bfc91bb67aca2f0758c4e4166ac242"]},"form":"Übermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["child","affirmation","innocence-play","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Над всеми вещами стоит небо случая, невинности и дерзновения.","en":"Chance’s, innocence’s and exuberance’s sky is affirmed above things."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.04","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-b7fb10245baaf5a19c74a9a76668ad78","tos.text-unit.sid-b7fb10245baaf5a19c74a9a76668ad78"]},"form":"Übermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-f42e08610d35c0b474f41b33b0abd201","tos.text-unit.sid-f42e08610d35c0b474f41b33b0abd201"]},"form":"muthwillt","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","laughter","body-self","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-aa3875e3a116520590e1579040fd316c","tos.text-unit.sid-aa3875e3a116520590e1579040fd316c"]},"form":"muthwilligen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","agency","joy-lust","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Все хорошие весёлые вещи прыгают от радости в бытие.","en":"All good, merry things leap into existence from joy."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6ff74fd54ade6148a224c2059fdfdbc1","tos.text-unit.sid-6ff74fd54ade6148a224c2059fdfdbc1"]},"form":"muthwilliges","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","identity","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9de6e207f7e40a794bcc8f8a99bd7023","tos.text-unit.sid-9de6e207f7e40a794bcc8f8a99bd7023"]},"form":"Muthwillen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","identity","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5529c712548623ecd7bdb53768ca2f01","tos.text-unit.sid-5529c712548623ecd7bdb53768ca2f01"]},"form":"Muthwillens","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-ae3aae794b18bd794f485722eeab56cf","tos.text-unit.sid-ae3aae794b18bd794f485722eeab56cf"]},"form":"Muthwille","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-980a7c471d6bb718893eb7f0681ea638","tos.text-unit.sid-980a7c471d6bb718893eb7f0681ea638"]},"form":"tapferen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["becoming","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.08","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-e3243f1b490b9f5b2a1a4388fc85a23d","tos.text-unit.sid-e3243f1b490b9f5b2a1a4388fc85a23d"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Смелость и пыл, долго сохраняющиеся в сердце, поддерживают настойчивость духа.","en":"Lasting courage sustains the spirit’s patience."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.09","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-25ae6a6396abe295325775e454ce39c3","tos.text-unit.sid-25ae6a6396abe295325775e454ce39c3"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"loneliness","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"quoted","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["loneliness","quietest-hour"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-fc56c359241358e2addbb61c545148d9","tos.text-unit.sid-fc56c359241358e2addbb61c545148d9"]},"form":"Muthwillen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","becoming","identity","dance","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Становление кажется божественной пляской и шалостью.","en":"Becoming is experienced as the gods’ dance and exuberance."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-ff728226990b4c1faa3f0c45c1ea0c7f","tos.text-unit.sid-ff728226990b4c1faa3f0c45c1ea0c7f"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["attention","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Окончить стихи требует большего мужества, чем продолжать их.","en":"Ending a poem takes more courage than continuing it."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-a41703696263cb43682abbc722ff3583","tos.text-unit.sid-a41703696263cb43682abbc722ff3583"]},"form":"Tapfere","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6fcd0214744f764ca02e3f41318946a0","tos.text-unit.sid-6fcd0214744f764ca02e3f41318946a0"]},"form":"Tapfere","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["will","identity","agency","earth","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-460172a31b9e34e5a3ceaa1cd1ac7108","tos.text-unit.sid-460172a31b9e34e5a3ceaa1cd1ac7108"]},"form":"Unmuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9ea66ba60295f130f6297ce69d0bd08b","tos.text-unit.sid-9ea66ba60295f130f6297ce69d0bd08b"]},"form":"Tapferen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.12","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-18f2de392aba4cb80aeb7c92adc36178","tos.text-unit.sid-18f2de392aba4cb80aeb7c92adc36178"]},"form":"Tapferkeit","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Порой храбрее пройти мимо, сохраняя себя для более достойного врага.","en":"Courage preserves strength for a worthy opponent."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-e8e279e1df353941f741c0cb295429e6","tos.text-unit.sid-e8e279e1df353941f741c0cb295429e6"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra-soul","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["becoming","zarathustra","zarathustra-soul"],"line":{"ru":"Подаривший всё душе встречает вопрос о благодарности.","en":"Having given everything to the soul, the giver meets the question of gratitude."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-e9cd4e260da6e891781003239a5ed23a","tos.text-unit.sid-e9cd4e260da6e891781003239a5ed23a"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra-soul","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["identity","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-6d591bed8717069d8de37a902e7980c7","tos.text-unit.sid-6d591bed8717069d8de37a902e7980c7"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra-soul","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["will","becoming","identity","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-e89b916963693a98598afe27a6c8c983","tos.text-unit.sid-e89b916963693a98598afe27a6c8c983"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra-soul","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"III.15","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-edfb6bf2039484d5b8b3b3532842999a","tos.text-unit.sid-880ace304e05292b1a76dc046e5ebca0"]},"form":"Übermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"life","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["identity","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Падение танцора вызывает просьбу о более ласковых путях.","en":"The dancer’s fall elicits a plea for gentler paths."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.03","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-9e286f5eb67a7cd3db864cb700cc3f39","tos.text-unit.sid-9e286f5eb67a7cd3db864cb700cc3f39"]},"form":"Tapfer","speaker":"kings","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["kings"],"line":{"ru":"Короли повторяют воинское определение храбрости как добра.","en":"The kings repeat the martial definition of bravery as good."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-8a8698a093651c087a2efd29ebb8d5c0","tos.text-unit.sid-8a8698a093651c087a2efd29ebb8d5c0"]},"form":"unvermuthetes","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"neighbour-words","neighbours":["present","identity","difference","gateway"],"line":{"ru":"Случайный взгляд папы превращает уклонение учителя во встречу.","en":"The pope’s chance glance turns the teacher’s evasion into an encounter."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.06","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-79cf3abc647caba19a4a644838212cc5","tos.text-unit.sid-79cf3abc647caba19a4a644838212cc5"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"last-pope","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель говорит папе, что слишком слаб, чтобы снять его тоску с плеч.","en":"The teacher tells the pope he is too weak to take the melancholy from his shoulders."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.07","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-0c93da67f6e0696d2f10528efa569a77","tos.text-unit.sid-0c93da67f6e0696d2f10528efa569a77"]},"form":"Muthe","speaker":"ugliest-man","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["ugliest-man"],"line":{"ru":"Убийца Бога узнаёт понимание своего состояния.","en":"God’s murderer recognizes understanding of his state."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.07","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-a592878f771efdf8dc6f638801885355","tos.text-unit.sid-a592878f771efdf8dc6f638801885355"]},"form":"Muthe","speaker":"ugliest-man","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["will","ugliest-man"],"line":{"ru":"Безобразный предлагает учителю иной путь ухода.","en":"The ugly one offers the teacher another way to leave."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-ac25338748b255e4f67972bbe236f187","tos.text-unit.sid-ac25338748b255e4f67972bbe236f187"]},"form":"muthwillig","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","zarathustra"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-7db6cedd3b6ce10bee1380d218531803","tos.text-unit.sid-7db6cedd3b6ce10bee1380d218531803"]},"form":"muthig","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["becoming","identity","agency","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Вид отчаявшегося бодрит: каждый считает себя достаточно сильным, чтобы его утешить.","en":"Seeing a despairing person heartens one: everyone considers themselves strong enough to comfort them."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-272becc64198e2b33244618ffb679506","tos.text-unit.sid-272becc64198e2b33244618ffb679506"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"kings","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","becoming","necessity","kings"],"line":{"ru":"Крик о помощи смолк; мысли и сердца открыты, а мужество скоро станет бодрым.","en":"The cry for help has ceased; thoughts and hearts are open, and courage will soon become cheerful."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.11","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-bfe5539571eb9d4f7c5bfec27f0da3a7","tos.text-unit.sid-bfe5539571eb9d4f7c5bfec27f0da3a7"]},"form":"Wohlgemuthere","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["lion","laughter","body-self","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель ждёт сильнейших и веселейших смеющихся львов.","en":"The teacher awaits stronger and more cheerful laughing lions."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.13","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-75bf49c544ff590fdea26d4cdf6002a8","tos.text-unit.sid-75bf49c544ff590fdea26d4cdf6002a8"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"question","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра спрашивает о мужестве отшельника и орла, которого не видят свидетели.","en":"Zarathustra asks about the courage of the hermit and eagle, unseen by witnesses."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.13","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-aed0d556529b97add13ff112c10e0b18","tos.text-unit.sid-aed0d556529b97add13ff112c10e0b18"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Мужество хватает бездну орлиным взглядом и когтями.","en":"Courage grasps the abyss with eagle eyes and claws."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.13","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-b9854c9add0c8fa76050e63cd64f2000","tos.text-unit.sid-b9854c9add0c8fa76050e63cd64f2000"]},"form":"Muths","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["identity","laughter","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра призывает учиться смеяться над собой.","en":"Zarathustra urges learning to laugh at oneself."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-5695c2f074d4a0165611aa4f076cbecd","tos.text-unit.sid-5695c2f074d4a0165611aa4f076cbecd"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"magician","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"song","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["magician"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-a961795f25b053df71ebcfe28a1c1672","tos.text-unit.sid-a961795f25b053df71ebcfe28a1c1672"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"magician","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"song","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["attention","magician"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.14","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-eb0c773a9f15394bb19d5e177c244834","tos.text-unit.sid-eb0c773a9f15394bb19d5e177c244834"]},"form":"Muthwillens","speaker":"magician","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","becoming","identity","memory","attention","laughter","ring","body-self","rope-bridge","earth","magician"],"line":{"ru":"Песнь чародея вспоминает жажду истины и называет поэта хищным, лживым зверем.","en":"The magician’s song recalls the thirst for truth and calls the poet a predatory, lying beast."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.15","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-fd282611c9229df57d4de0cb49aa9452","tos.text-unit.sid-fd282611c9229df57d4de0cb49aa9452"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"conscientious","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["joy-lust","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Заратустра видит мужество в первобытной истории человека, в духе приключений и любви к неизвестному.","en":"Zarathustra sees courage in human prehistory, in the spirit of adventure and love of the unknown."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.15","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-03febab1c54982fb8b23d513155f4c6d","tos.text-unit.sid-03febab1c54982fb8b23d513155f4c6d"]},"form":"muthigsten","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"conscientious","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["becoming","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Человек отнял добродетели у самых диких и мужественных животных и этим стал человеком.","en":"The human took the virtues of the wildest and bravest animals and thereby became human."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.15","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-db02e7c47cf3d047b82e366660a14334","tos.text-unit.sid-db02e7c47cf3d047b82e366660a14334"]},"form":"Muth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"conscientious","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["becoming","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Одухотворённое мужество соединяет крылья орла и мудрость змеи.","en":"Spiritualized courage joins eagle wings and serpent wisdom."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.16","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-8df6c6c254596dcd2319bad8e0cf8605","tos.text-unit.sid-8df6c6c254596dcd2319bad8e0cf8605"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"shadow","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["shadow"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.16","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-790eb0b59d19e807170bc19792238b61","tos.text-unit.sid-790eb0b59d19e807170bc19792238b61"]},"form":"Schwermuth","speaker":"shadow","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"dispositions","neighbours":["innocence-play","shadow"]},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.16","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-560c8e1bc5e590cf6443e36f4cc8d830","tos.text-unit.sid-560c8e1bc5e590cf6443e36f4cc8d830"]},"form":"Übermuthe","speaker":"shadow","addressee":"daughters","mode":"song","use":"song","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","lion","affirmation","identity","memory","difference","agency","bite","dance","loneliness","shadow"],"line":{"ru":"Тень поёт о льве и обезьяне — ревуне морали, называя себя европейцем.","en":"The shadow sings of the lion and the ape, a moral howler, calling himself a European."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.17","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1160053cb5021be807b8ed58a59225e4","tos.text-unit.sid-1160053cb5021be807b8ed58a59225e4"]},"form":"Ermuthigung","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"courage","neighbours":["will","becoming","identity","laughter"],"line":{"ru":"Радость гостей кажется Заратустре признаком их выздоровления.","en":"The guests’ joy seems to Zarathustra a sign of their recovery."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.17","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-cc1c1cfe64b5e306475fd437132d7b5a","tos.text-unit.sid-cc1c1cfe64b5e306475fd437132d7b5a"]},"form":"Muthwillen","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"zarathustra","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["will","becoming","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Новые надежды явились в руках и ногах гостей.","en":"New hope enters the guests’ hands and feet."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-b7ba576aa90365f535f7d718560a40bf","tos.text-unit.sid-b7ba576aa90365f535f7d718560a40bf"]},"form":"Übermuth","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"exuberance","neighbours":["child","zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Учитель выводит детское озорство из пещеры на воздух.","en":"The teacher leads childish exuberance from the cave into open air."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.18","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-1da1d7ea77e5beb63dd86311f40fefbb","tos.text-unit.sid-1da1d7ea77e5beb63dd86311f40fefbb"]},"form":"tapferer","speaker":"zarathustra","addressee":"higher-men","mode":"speech","use":"teaching","group":"courage","neighbours":["zarathustra"],"line":{"ru":"Праздничная нелепость изображена ветром, очищающим душу.","en":"Festive absurdity is pictured as a wind clearing the soul."}},{"cite":{"w":"also-sprach-zarathustra","c":"IV.19","u":["tos.text-unit.sid-93df51c08c74c1ca217075c344b20b95","tos.text-unit.sid-93df51c08c74c1ca217075c344b20b95"]},"form":"tapferen","speaker":"narrator","addressee":"","mode":"narration","use":"narration","group":"courage","neighbours":["identity","difference","earth"],"line":{"ru":"Ночная тишина приближает гостей к счастью земной жизни.","en":"Night’s silence brings the guests closer to earthly happiness."}}]}
